      "id": "v858ayb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning and Characteristics of Ocean Currents"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ocean currents are large-scale continuous movements of ocean water driven by wind, gravity, temperature, and density gradients.",
        "Ocean gyres form large circular current patterns in the Atlantic, Pacific, and Indian Oceans influenced by the Coriolis effect.",
        "Thermohaline circulation operates as a deep-ocean global conveyor belt transferring heat and nutrients worldwide.",
        "Upwelling brings cold, nutrient-rich deep water to the surface, supporting rich marine life and major fishing zones."
      ],
      "id": "6uu3vbd"
    },
